ter the quarterback looked better than anticipated in pregame warmups.","published":"2026-11-14T18:56:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480988/alabama-makes-last-second-call-start-qb-keelon-russell","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Maryland QB Malik Washington doesn't start vs. Wisconsin","description":"Maryland quarterback Malik Washington did not start against Wisconsin as he continues to deal with a lower-body injury.","published":"2026-11-14T17:50:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480722/source-maryland-qb-malik-washington-start-vs-wisconsin","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado upsets No. 14 Houston for first AP top-15 win since 2007","description":"Colorado posted its first victory over an AP top-15 team since 2007 in beating No. 14 Houston 42-32 and slightly cooled down the hot seat for coach Deion Sanders.","published":"2026-11-14T14:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50479172/colorado-upsets-no-14-houston-1st-ap-top-15-win-2007","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ole Miss-Oklahoma bumped to Sunday despite Sooners AD's 'strong objection'","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny was critical of the SEC's decision to move the Sooners' home game against Ole Miss to Sunday following Friday's nationwide ground stop.","published":"2026-11-14T17:36:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50478281/ole-miss-oklahoma-bumped-sunday-sooners-ad-rips-decision","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA QB Ty Dieffenbach says first-half shoulder injury vs. Illinois not serious","description":"UCLA starting quarterback Ty Dieffenbach exited because of a shoulder injury late in the second quarter but returned to lead the Bruins past Illinois 22-14.","published":"2026-11-14T17:06:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50477249/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-leaves-game-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest claims 'Bachelor U' status after Sam Hartman news","description":"Wake Forest football is the only program, the school says, to have had three former players feature in \"The Bachelor\" franchise.","published":"2026-11-13T23:57:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50475193/sam-hartman-bachelor-wake-forest","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":9,"round":1,"team":"ATL","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:53Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}